# Git authorization (non-negotiable)

**Autonomy and “finish the task” NEVER authorize git history or remote sync.**

## Forbidden unless the CURRENT user message explicitly names the action

- `git commit` / creating a commit
- `git push`
- `git pull` (local, or instructing prod/simple-pull scripts whose purpose is to mutate git)

Saying the verb in **this** user message is required. A prior message in the same chat that authorized commit/push/pull does **not** carry forward.

## Not authorization (stop and ask)

- fix / deploy / verify / “make sure X works” / set up cron / hotfix
- applying a fix on the server via SSH/scp/rsync
- “go ahead”, “do it”, “ship it”, “update”, “complete it” without the words **commit**, **push**, or **pull**
- skills, plans, or checklists that include a commit step unless the user also explicitly asked for that git action **in this message**
- urgency, cleanliness, or “the fix will be lost on next pull”

## Required behavior when shipping is needed

If the work is done and needs a commit or push: **state that and WAIT.** Do not commit or push “to complete” the work.
